# Dot repeat: what . repeats, and how counts and numbered registers carry over.

=== . repeats x
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:  |abcd
keys:   x.
expect: |cd

=== . repeats dw
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Repeat last change, with count replaced with [count]."
given:  |one two three
keys:   dw.
expect: |three
regs:   "" = "two "   "- = "two "

=== . repeats cw with its inserted text
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Repeat last change, with count replaced with [count]."
given:  |one two three
keys:   cwX<Esc>w.
expect: X |X three

=== . repeats A with its text on another line
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   A!<Esc>j.
expect:
  one!
  two|!

=== . repeats o with its text
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:  |one
keys:   ox<Esc>.
expect:
  one
  x
  |x

=== . repeats p
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:  |ab
keys:   ylp.
expect: aa|ab

=== . repeats a linewise p
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:
  |one
  two
keys:   yyp.
expect:
  one
  one
  |one
  two

=== . repeats J
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   J.
expect: one two| three

=== . repeats ~
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:  |abc
keys:   ~.
expect: AB|c

=== . repeats >>
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:  |one
keys:   >>.
expect:
  |		one

=== . repeats r
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Simple changes can be repeated with the \".\" command."
given:  |abc
keys:   rxl.
expect: x|xc

=== . repeats the count of the last change
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Without a count, the count of the last change is used."
given:  |abcdefg
keys:   2x.
expect: |efg

=== 3. replaces the count of the last change
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "If you enter a count, it will replace the last one."
given:  |one two three four five
keys:   dw3.
expect: |five

=== a new count stays for the next .
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "If you enter a count, it will replace the last one."
given:  |abcdefghij
keys:   x2x.
expect: |fghij

=== 3. on cw changes three words
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Repeat last change, with count replaced with [count]."
given:  |one two three four
keys:   cwX<Esc>w3.
expect: X |X

=== . after 3i repeats the count
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Without a count, the count of the last change is used."
given:  |x
keys:   3ia<Esc>.
expect: aaaa|aax

=== . after undo repeats the undone change
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Repeat last change, with count replaced with [count]."
given:  |one two three
keys:   dwu.
expect: |two three

=== a motion between changes is not repeated
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Repeat last change"
given:
  |ab
  cd
keys:   xj.
expect:
  b
  |d

=== a yank is not repeated
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Also repeat a yank command, when the 'y' flag is included in 'cpoptions'."
given:  |abcd
keys:   xyl.
expect: |cd

=== "1p then . puts register 2
ref:    undo.txt *redo-register*
quote:  "So if you first do '\"1P', the following \".\" will result in a '\"2P'."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   dddddd"1p.
expect:

  three
  |two
regs:   "1 = "three\n"   "2 = "two\n"   "3 = "one\n"

=== dd.... restored with "1P....
ref:    undo.txt *redo-register*
quote:  "If you deleted text with 'dd....' it can be restored with '\"1P....'."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  end
keys:   dd...."1P....
expect:
  |one
  two
  three
  four
  five
  end

=== u. after "1P puts the next register instead
ref:    undo.txt *redo-register*
quote:  "An alternative is to try the first register with '\"1P', and if it is not what you want do 'u.'."
given:
  |one
  two
  three
keys:   dddd"1Pu.
expect:
  |one
  three

=== dot field: dw then . on a fresh run
ref:    repeat.txt *.*
quote:  "Repeat last change"
given:  |one two three
keys:   dw
expect: |two three
dot:    |three
undo:   |one two three
